    "danger": 3,
    "formed_by": "builder",
    "resident": "the Unwritten, the clanless who are grinding their own names out of the Long Tally, and Kadda the Rasp at its head",
    "story": "Dunnow's halls climb into the Wall a storey at a time, every wall of every hall cut with the Long Tally from the floor to as high as a cutter could reach on a ladder: the oldest prices at the door, the newest at the top, the year cut at the head of each wall. The keepers' rest, their store, the gallery where the chain of the Chain Years crosses a cleft in the rock, and at the top the hall where the tally ends, with a wall left blank for the debts to come. The Unwritten sleep in the keepers' beds and work by torchlight, a rasp in every hand.",
    "unique_object": "the blank wall at the head of the hold, which the keepers left for the debts to come, and on which Kadda has begun to cut, very carefully, a tally of the names the Unwritten have ground away",
