    "resident": "crag-wolves denning in the old upper level, scree-hags in the ladderways, stone-thralls that walked out of the seam, and at the bottom the Chained Brakh, still in the chain the last shift put on it",
    "story": "The shaft goes down to the upper level, where the first Brindle followed the red vein along the fell with picks; then a ladderway to the deep levels, where the iron got richer and redder, the drawing forge where they made chain underground because the iron would not keep its temper in daylight, and the break where the last shift's picks went through into the giant's marrow. Past the break the seam is bone, not stone, and the timbering stops.",
    "unique_object": "the last shift's tally of iron, chalked on a timber at the drawing forge: forty-one hundredweight in the week before the break, and in the week after, in the same hand, a figure so much larger that somebody has since scratched it out",
