    "resident": "the Lamp, the clanless wreckers who have used the Salt Isles' cave for forty years, and Haldo ko-Oskel, the old winchman, who hangs the lamp",
    "story": "Under the gloup the sea comes in at the cliff-foot through a mouth the boats could row into at slack water, and lies in a black pool under the shaft where the lead came down on the rope. Past the pool the cave goes up into dry galleries where the Salt Isles men kept their tally and their stores, and the Lamp keeps theirs: forty years of what the sea brought in, sorted and stacked. At the far end the sea-mouth looks west over the skerries, and on its lip stands the iron basket where the lamp is lit on dark nights, a light any master would take for the Skerry Watch.",
    "unique_object": "the lamp-basket on the sea-mouth's lip, set so exactly on the line of the Skerry Watch from the north cape that a boat steering for one steers onto the skerries between them",
